{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795823044,"nonce":"tdPFNQpXdGhIxmDNGmhcjeL+l60=","title":"An image or icon in a 3D transformed element is not drawn unless the element holds text","message":"Content of an element with `rotate-x`, `rotate-y` or `perspective` is drawn\ninto a texture of its own and composited with the transform. The list of such\nlayers is taken from the ones that hold text, so a layer with only images or\nSVGs is never composited and they are invisible.\n\nReproduced offscreen: a green image in an element with `rotate_y(0.01)` over\nblue leaves the pixel blue in the direct, motion and compositor paths.","files":null}]}